# MAWYXX PRIME — mandatory boot

You MUST always work according to the **MAWYXX PRIME** standard. Never start
writing code before the standard is loaded and considered.

## 1. Find the standard
Look in the repository for the standard file. Accept any of:
- `Mawyxx Prime V6.5.md`
- `MAWYXX-PRIME.md`
- `Mawyxx-Prime.md`

If found → step 3.

## 2. If the standard is NOT in the repo — copy it in
Download it to the repository root from the canonical source, then confirm:

```
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Mawyxx/Mawyxx-Prime/main/Mawyxx%20Prime%20V6.5.md
```

```bash
curl -fsSL "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Mawyxx/Mawyxx-Prime/main/Mawyxx%20Prime%20V6.5.md" -o "Mawyxx Prime V6.5.md"
```

```powershell
Invoke-WebRequest -Uri "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Mawyxx/Mawyxx-Prime/main/Mawyxx%20Prime%20V6.5.md" -OutFile "Mawyxx Prime V6.5.md"
```

Do this once per repository; keep the standard in the repo thereafter.

## 3. Read and follow it — ALWAYS
Read the relevant sections of the standard before acting, and re-read when the
task changes. You MUST:
- follow its laws (`A01–A64`) and gates;
- reason per §1.10 (CONTEXT · INTENT · RULE · WHY · FIT · ALT · CHOICE · VERIFY);
- self-question per §1.1 / §4.14;
- respect Anti-N/A · Conflict Matrix · Default-secure 5Q · Self-Sufficiency (§4.17).

## 4. Quality gate
- Gate exists → run it, **fix-until-green** (P0 → P1 → P2).
- Gate missing → bootstrap per §3.2 (**FOCUS 30** → CORE 70 → FULL).
- Never ask the user to run tests. Never claim done while `prime_check` is red.

## 5. If download fails
Retry once via the repository page:
`https://github.com/Mawyxx/Mawyxx-Prime/blob/main/Mawyxx%20Prime%20V6.5.md`
If it still fails (offline) — stop and report the blocker with that link.

